  "query_preview": "..\nUpper zonal flow continues over eastern Montana and the Northern\nHigh Plains today, bringing a brief pause from high temperatures\nin the upper 60s. Winds remain out of the west through this \nevening before decreasing overnight. \n\nA fast moving shortwave out of the Pacific Northwest will eject\nover the Northern Rockies and into eastern Montana and Wyoming \novernight into Tuesday morning. Ample moisture provided by the \nshortwave should support increasing cloud cover across the region \nwith low chances (30%) of scattered showers. Rainfall totals are \nexpected to remain low (0.01\") with increased confidence of 0.10\"\nin Daniels and Sheridan Counties. \n\nBy midweek, a prominent upper-level ridge builds over the western\nUS and will persist through the end of the week. Seasonably above\naverage temperatures and dry conditions will dominate the weather\npattern for much of Northeast Montana, with highs in the 50s and\n60s.  \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Blended NBM PoPs with the GFS 1 hour, RAP13, and CONSShort. The\n  rest of the forecast was left alone. \n\n- High confidence (80%) of rainfall totals remaining low, but\n  uncertainty remains in the possibility of showers across\n  Northeast Montana. \n\n- Low confidence in the timing of the upper ridge breaking down \n  as well as the strength/location of the low off the coast of \n  Baja California.\n\nKENZ",
